Minato's patch to frameworks/base's media/java/android/media/ImageReader.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0), the
graphics breadth's G3a (ADR-0058 e1)): the static initializer loads no libmedia_jni.

Why: Android's ImageReader natives live in libmedia_jni, which its static initializer loads. Minato builds no
libmedia_jni; its ImageReader natives are libandroid_runtime's (framework/native/android_runtime/
android_media_ImageReader.cpp), registered with the framework's others when the process starts, so the load would
throw UnsatisfiedLinkError out of <clinit> and every use of the class would fail. nativeClassInit stays.

--- a/media/java/android/media/ImageReader.java
+++ b/media/java/android/media/ImageReader.java
@@ -1513,7 +1513,7 @@
      */
     private static native void nativeClassInit();
     static {
-        System.loadLibrary("media_jni");
+        // Minato: the natives are libandroid_runtime's (android_media_ImageReader.cpp), registered at the start.
         nativeClassInit();
     }
 }
